Intel(R) Graphics Compute Runtime headers - fetched at build time from public upstream.

Component:   compute-runtime headers: OpenCL tracing and private extension
             headers (tracing_api.h, tracing_types.h, cl_ext_private.h) and
             Intel Level Zero extension headers (ze_stypes.h, ze_intel_gpu.h,
             driver_experimental/zex_*.h)
Upstream:    https://github.com/intel/compute-runtime
Version:     pinned by the commit in tools/unitrace/scripts/get_compute_runtime_headers.py,
             the single source of truth (not repeated here)
License:     MIT (see ./LICENSE)

How it is used: scripts/get_compute_runtime_headers.py clones compute-runtime at
the pinned commit and copies the headers into the build tree; unitrace compiles
against them.

To bump: update the commit in get_compute_runtime_headers.py, refresh LICENSE
from upstream (LICENSE.md) at the new commit, and update
tools/unitrace/third-party-programs.txt if the license or copyright changed.
